  "repo": "swesmith/pallets__click.fde47b4b",
  "problem_statement": "Stream compatibility check broken for stdin and stderr handling\n\n#### Description\n\nThe stream compatibility check in `_is_compat_stream_attr` is not working correctly, causing issues with stdin/stderr handling in Click's testing utilities and progress bars.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport click\nfrom click.testing import CliRunner\n\n@click.command()\n@click.argument('f', type=click.File())\ndef cli(f):\n    click.echo(f.name)\n    click.echo(f.mode, nl=False)\n\nrunner = CliRunner()\nresult = runner.invoke(cli, ['-'])\nprint(f\"Expected: '<stdin>\\\\nr'\")\nprint(f\"Actual: '{result.output}'\")\n```\n\nAlso affects stderr isolation:\n\n```python\nfrom click.testing import CliRunner\nimport click\n\nrunner = CliRunner()\nwith runner.isolation() as (_, err, _):\n    click.echo('\\udce2', err=True, nl=False)\nprint(f\"Expected: b'\\\\\\\\udce2'\")\nprint(f\"Actual: {err.getvalue()}\")\n```\n\nAnd progress bar display:\n\n```python\nimport click\nfrom click.testing import CliRunner\n\n@click.command()\ndef cli():\n    with click.progressbar(range(4)) as progress:\n        for _ in progress:\n            print('')\n\nrunner = CliRunner()\nresult = runner.invoke(cli, [])\n# Progress bar output is malformed\n```\n\nThe stream compatibility logic appears to be inverted, causing streams to be incorrectly identified as incompatible when they should be compatible."
}